  "<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Solitude and Last Horizon</a> both ship with Omarchy, and another twenty of his themes sit on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a> - more than anyone else has contributed: Batou, Oxo Carbon, Velvet Night, Rose of Dune, Shades of Jade, and on it goes. He&rsquo;s a mechanical engineer who became one of the defining aesthetic forces in this community, sits on <a href=\"/teams/\">Omarchy Core</a>, and helps steward <a href=\"https://plugins.omarchy.org/\">the plugin ecosystem</a>.": "<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Solitude 與 Last Horizon</a>都隨 Omarchy 出貨，他的另外二十套佈景主題放在<a href=\"/themes/\">附錄頁面</a>——無人能出其右：Batou、Oxo Carbon、Velvet Night、Rose of Dune、Shades of Jade，等等。他是機械工程師出身，如今是這個社群最具代表性的美學推手之一，擔任<a href=\"/teams/\">Omarchy Core</a> 成員，並協助打理<a href=\"https://plugins.omarchy.org/\">外掛生態系</a>。",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-exclusive-hyprland-sponsor/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://hypr.land/\">Hyprland</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/vaxryy\">Vaxry</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-exclusive-hyprland-sponsor/\">閱讀公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://hypr.land/\">Hyprland</a>，作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/vaxryy\">Vaxry</a>",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-premier-mise-sponsor/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://mise.jdx.dev/\">mise</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/jdxcode\">jdx</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-premier-mise-sponsor/\">閱讀公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://mise.jdx.dev/\">mise</a>，作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/jdxcode\">jdx</a>",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/09/omacom-foundation-hires-outfoxxed/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/outfoxxedd\">outfoxxed</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/09/omacom-foundation-hires-outfoxxed/\">閱讀公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a>，作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/outfoxxedd\">outfoxxed</a>",
  "<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">Become a patron</a> to claim yours. Artwork by <a href=\"https://github.com/OldJobobo\">OldJobobo</a>, <a href=\"/air/\">Artist in Residence</a>.": "<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">成為贊助者</a>即可領取你的徽章。插畫由<a href=\"https://github.com/OldJobobo\">OldJobobo</a> 繪製，<a href=\"/air/\">駐站藝術家</a>。",
  "<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">Elite capital. Public code.</a>": "<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">菁英資本。公開程式碼。</a>",
  "<span><strong>$2,500/month</strong> for the full six months.</span>": "<span><strong>2,500 USD/月</strong>，連續六個月。</span>",
  "<span><strong>Permanent recognition</strong> as AIR alumni when six months are up.</span>": "<span><strong>永久表彰</strong>，六個月期滿即成為 AIR 校友。</span>",
  "<span><strong>Token account</strong> so the agents never need to stop.</span>": "<span><strong>代幣帳戶</strong>，讓代理永不停歇。</span>",
  "A 2011 ThinkPad X220. Just 2GB of RAM. Watch Omarchy run with room to spare.": "一台 2011 年的 ThinkPad X220，只有 2GB 記憶體。看 Omarchy 跑得綽綽有餘。",
  "A six-month residency for artists who make Omarchy beautiful. Themes, plugins, and whatever else. The point is to let creativity flow with the support of the Omacom Foundation. Up to five seats at any one time.": "為期六個月的駐站計畫，獻給讓 Omarchy 變美麗的藝術家。佈景主題、外掛，以及其他一切。重點是在 Omacom Foundation 的支持下，讓創意自由流動。同時最多五個名額。",
  "An explanation of what an attacker can do before and after exploitation.": "關於攻擊者在入侵前後能做什麼的說明。",
  "Artists in Residence": "駐站藝術家",
  "Avoid privacy violations, disruption, data destruction, and service degradation.": "避免侵犯隱私、干擾他人、破壞資料與降低服務品質。",
  "Blue foil and a dusty hairpin high up the mountain. This is the class for those who want to put some real weight behind the mission.": "藍色箔面，高山上的多塵髮夾彎。這個級別獻給想為使命真正出份力的人。",
  "But it also found the ceiling. Omakub was a layer of opinion on top of Ubuntu and GNOME, and those come with strong opinions of their own. The ideas I actually cared about - tiling, everything on the keyboard, a system that treats the terminal as the center of the universe - kept fighting the platform instead of flowing from it.": "但它也撞到了天花板。Omakub 是疊在 Ubuntu 與 GNOME 之上的一層主張，而它們自己主張也很強。我真正在乎的想法——平鋪、一切都用鍵盤、把終端機當成宇宙中心的系統——一直在跟平台打架，而不是從平台自然長出來。",
  "Code that could be more robust but does not cross a security boundary is an improvement rather than a security vulnerability. We may still merge a proposed fix and credit the reporter in our release notes.": "程式碼可以更強健，但只要沒有跨越安全邊界，就是改進而非安全漏洞。我們仍可能合併你提的修法，並在版本說明中致謝。",
  "Coming 2026": "2026 年登場",
  "Credits": "致謝",
  "Credits link to each reporter&rsquo;s X profile and show their avatar. For duplicate reports, only the first reporter is eligible for credit.": "致謝會連結到每位回報者的 X 個人檔案並顯示大頭貼。若有重複回報，只有第一位回報者能獲得致謝。",
  "David Heinemeier Hansson takes Omarchy for a spin on a very modest machine.": "David Heinemeier Hansson 在一台非常陽春的機器上試駕 Omarchy。",
  "Don&rsquo;t exploit a vulnerability beyond what is needed to demonstrate it.": "展示漏洞時，不要超出必要範圍去利用它。",
  "Each contributing $1,000,000.": "每位贊助 1,000,000 USD。",
  "Each contributing $1,000,000/year for three years or $1,500,000 in tokens with option for refill.": "每位每年贊助 1,000,000 USD，為期三年，或 1,500,000 USD 代幣，可補充。",
  "Each contributing $100,000.": "每位贊助 100,000 USD。",
  "Each contributing $100,000/year for three years or $150,000 in tokens with option for refill.": "每位每年贊助 100,000 USD，為期三年，或 150,000 USD 代幣，可補充。",
  "Each contributing $16 or more.": "每位贊助 16 USD（含）以上。",
  "Each contributing $2,048 or more.": "每位贊助 2,048 USD（含）以上。",
  "Each contributing $256 or more.": "每位贊助 256 USD（含）以上。",
  "Each contributing $8,192 or more.": "每位贊助 8,192 USD（含）以上。",
  "Each contributing as they see fit. Open for everyone.<br><a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">Become a patron</a> and <a href=\"/patrons/badges/\">collect your badge</a>.": "金額隨心，歡迎所有人。<br><a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">成為贊助者</a>並<a href=\"/patrons/badges/\">領取你的徽章</a>。",
  "Early Aesthetics": "早期美學",
  "Eligibility for our <a href=\"/security/credits/\">security credits</a> page depends on whether a report identifies a confirmed security vulnerability, not on its severity.": "能否登上我們的<a href=\"/security/credits/\">安全致謝</a>頁面，取決於回報是否指出經確認的安全漏洞，而與嚴重程度無關。",
  "Emir built <a href=\"https://tryomarchy.dev/\">TryOmarchy</a> and <a href=\"https://isorun.ai/\">Isorun</a>, drawing on more than twenty years with Linux and nearly seven years in Booking.com&rsquo;s SRE department. He leads the infrastructure that builds, tests, and ships Omarchy as it expands to more hardware and architectures, and serves on <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a>.": "Emir 打造了<a href=\"https://tryomarchy.dev/\">TryOmarchy</a> 與 <a href=\"https://isorun.ai/\">Isorun</a>，擁有二十多年 Linux 經驗，並在 Booking.com 的 SRE 部門待了近七年。他領導建構、測試與出貨 Omarchy 的基礎設施，隨它擴展到更多硬體與架構，並擔任<a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a> 成員。",
  "Even then, one command could re-theme multiple apps.": "即便如此，一道指令就能為多個應用換膚。",
  "Every patron of the Omacom Foundation gets a digital rally credential to show for it. There's a badge for your website, a card for your socials, and wallpapers for your desktop and your phone. Four classes, one for each <a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">tier of patronage</a>. Pick your stage!": "每位 Omacom Foundation 贊助者都能獲得一枚數位集會徽章。網站用的徽章、社群用的卡片、桌機與手機用的桌布，四個級別，對應<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">四級贊助</a>。選你的賽段吧！",
  "Excellence is not born out of committee, and Omarchy is not a democracy. It&#39;s a benevolent dictatorship in the grand tradition of Linux, Ruby, and Rails. The dictator&#39;s job is to listen to everyone, but make the call according to their intuition, vision, and experience. Some calls will be wrong, and then they&#39;ll be reverted. Others will be delegated. But the buck will always have a place to stop.": "卓越不是開會開出來的，Omarchy 也不是民主國家。它是承襲 Linux、Ruby、Rails 偉大傳統的仁慈獨裁。獨裁者的工作是聽每個人的，但憑直覺、願景與經驗拍板。有些決定會錯，錯了就撤回；有些會授權出去。但責任永遠有地方落。",
  "Exclusive": "獨家",
  "For anything that isn&rsquo;t a security vulnerability, please use the <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues\">Omarchy issue tracker</a>.": "任何非安全漏洞的事項，請使用<a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues\">Omarchy 問題追蹤器</a>。",
  "Forest Stage &middot; $16": "Forest Stage &middot; 16 USD",
  "Found something? <a href=\"/security/\">Report it privately</a>. The first reporter of a confirmed vulnerability is credited here.": "有發現？<a href=\"/security/\">私下回報</a>。經確認的漏洞的第一位回報者會在此獲得致謝。",
  "Full-time Omacom Foundation employee": "Omacom Foundation 全職員工",
  "Give us a reasonable opportunity to investigate and address the issue before publishing details.": "公開細節前，請給我們合理的時間調查與處理。",
  "Give us enough information to understand and reproduce the issue:": "提供足夠資訊，讓我們理解並重現問題：",
  "Great tools are beautiful because they&#39;re right. The best curve of the blade is also the elegant one, so let&#39;s nail the sharp lines of that TUI, get those corner radii right, and polish the CLIs. The colors should be coordinated. The padding should be just so. There&#39;s enough desaturated brutalism in this world already. Make it shine, make it wow, make it art.": "好工具之所以美，是因為它正確。刀鋒最美的弧線也是最優雅的那一道，所以讓我們把 TUI 的俐落線條釘好，把圓角調對，把 CLI 磨亮。顏色要協調，留白要剛好。這世界去飽和的粗野主義已經夠多了。讓它發光，讓它驚豔，讓它成藝術。",
  "He drew the Omarchy logo, which is reason enough, and he built <a href=\"https://github.com/tahayvr/omarchist\">Omarchist</a>, the GUI for making your own themes without touching a config file. <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Matte Black</a> is his and ships with Omarchy, along with Gold Rush, Sunset Drive, and VHS 80 on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a>.": "他畫了 Omarchy 標誌，光這點就夠了；他還打造了<a href=\"https://github.com/tahayvr/omarchist\">Omarchist</a>——不用碰設定檔就能自製佈景主題的 GUI。<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Matte Black</a> 是他的作品，隨 Omarchy 出貨，Gold Rush、Sunset Drive、VHS 80 也在<a href=\"/themes/\">附錄頁面</a>上。",
  "Head of Infrastructure": "基礎設施主管",
  "Head of Omarchy Kernel": "Omarchy 核心主管",
  "Head of Omarchy Shell": "Omarchy Shell 主管",
  "If you believe you&rsquo;ve found a security vulnerability in Omarchy, please tell the <a href=\"/teams/#security\">Omarchy Security Team</a> privately so we have an opportunity to investigate and fix it before it is made public.": "如果你認為在 Omarchy 發現了安全漏洞，請私下告訴<a href=\"/teams/#security\">Omarchy 安全團隊</a>，讓我們有機會在公開前調查並修復。",
  "Interested in becoming a founding or distinguished patron? Write <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>.": "想成為創始或傑出贊助者？寫信至 <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "Krzysztof co-maintains key parts of Linux&rsquo;s PCI subsystem. His work helps the kernel communicate with modern hardware, from graphics cards to fast storage. He leads Omarchy Kernel performance, compatibility, and security, and serves on <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a>.": "Krzysztof 共同維護 Linux 的 PCI 子系統關鍵部分。他的工作幫助核心與現代硬體溝通，從顯示卡到高速儲存。他領導 Omarchy 核心的效能、相容性與安全，並擔任<a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a> 成員。",
  "Logo": "標誌",
  "Magenta foil, four headlights, and a night stage carved out of the mountainside. The top class of open patronage. Thank you!": "維修區燈光下的洋紅色箔面，賽車在站與站之間於此重建。開放贊助的最高級別。謝謝！",
  "Mountain Hairpin &middot; $256": "Mountain Hairpin &middot; 256 USD",
  "Multi-year sponsorships for the projects Omarchy is built on - Hyprland and mise - so the people behind them can work without thinking about fundraising.": "給 Omarchy 背後專案——Hyprland 與 mise——的多年期贊助，讓背後的人不必為募款操心，專心工作。",
  "Neovim and Zellij out of the box.": "Neovim 與 Zellij，開箱即有。",
  "Night Stage &middot; $8,192": "Night Stage &middot; 8,192 USD",
  "OMA Logo": "OMA 標誌",
  "Omakub itself is now retired. The repositories are archived on GitHub - <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub\">omakub</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub-site\">omakub-site</a>. But good ideas don&rsquo;t retire, they get forked! <a href=\"https://omabuntu.omakasui.org/\">Omabuntu</a> is a community fork continuing on the omakase-Ubuntu thread. If Arch is a step too far and Ubuntu is home, that&rsquo;s where you should go.": "Omakub 本人已經退休。程式碼庫在 GitHub 上封存——<a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub\">omakub</a> 與 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub-site\">omakub-site</a>。但好想法不退休，只會被複刻！<a href=\"https://omabuntu.omakasui.org/\">Omabuntu</a> 是社群 fork，延續 omakase-Ubuntu 這條線。如果 Arch 跨太大步、Ubuntu 才是家，就去那裡吧。",
  "Omakub proved the thesis: give developers a beautiful, complete Linux out of the box, and they&rsquo;ll show up! Tens of thousands did.": "Omakub 證明了論點：給開發者一個開箱即用、美麗完整的 Linux，他們就會來！數萬人都來了。",
  "Omarchy AIR pays artists a six-month stipend to work freely on themes, plugins, and whatever else makes the system beautiful.": "Omarchy AIR 發給藝術家六個月津貼，讓他們自由創作佈景主題、外掛，以及任何讓系統變美麗的東西。",
  "Omarchy is a pending trademark. All rights reserved.": "Omarchy 是申請中的商標。版權所有。",
  "Omarchy is for everyone willing to learn and participate. From <a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">billionaires</a> to anons on X. From <a href=\"/staff\">staff engineers</a> to script kiddies. From <a href=\"https://omarchy.cn\">China</a> to Malibu. Show up, fix something, or just spread the enthusiasm. <a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2097747649625497874\">You&#39;re somebody now</a>.": "只要願意學、願意參與，Omarchy 就屬於每個人。從<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">億萬富翁</a>到 X 上的匿名帳號。從<a href=\"/staff\">員工工程師</a>到腳本小子。從<a href=\"https://omarchy.cn\">中國</a>到 Malibu。來吧，修點東西，或散播熱情也好。<a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2097747649625497874\">你現在可是個人物了</a>。",
  "Only test systems and accounts you own or have explicit permission to test.": "只測試你擁有或已獲明確授權測試的系統與帳號。",
  "Patrons": "贊助者",
  "Please act in good faith while investigating and reporting vulnerabilities:": "調查與回報漏洞時請秉持善意：",
  "Please don&rsquo;t report potential vulnerabilities publicly in GitHub Issues, Discord, or social media before they&rsquo;ve been resolved.": "在問題解決前，請勿在 GitHub Issues、Discord 或社群媒體上公開回報可能的漏洞。",
  "Premier": "首席",
  "Quickshell is the desktop construction kit behind Omarchy Shell. It provides the building blocks for bars, menus, notifications, widgets, and lock screens, using QML to turn ideas into interfaces that update as you work. That flexibility lets people and their agents build plugins and shape the desktop around their needs. Its creator, outfoxxed, is a full-time Omacom Foundation employee as Head of Omarchy Shell and a member of Omarchy Core, working to make the shell and its foundations faster, more reliable, and easier to extend.": "Quickshell 是 Omarchy Shell 背後的桌面建造套件。它為狀態列、選單、通知、小工具與鎖定畫面提供建材，用 QML 把想法變成會隨工作即時更新的介面。這份彈性讓人們和他們的代理能打造外掛、把桌面捏成自己需要的樣子。它的創造者 outfoxxed 是 Omacom Foundation 全職員工，擔任 Omarchy Shell 主管與 Omarchy Core 成員，讓 shell 及其根基更快、更可靠、更好擴展。",
  "Regular bugs and support": "一般 bug 與支援",
  "Remaining seats by invitation": "剩餘名額僅限邀請",
  "Report a vulnerability": "回報漏洞",
  "Researchers who privately report a confirmed security vulnerability and give us the chance to ship a fix are thanked on the <a href=\"/security/credits/\">security credits</a> page. Accepted improvements that don&rsquo;t cross a security boundary may still be credited in our release notes.": "私下回報經確認的安全漏洞、讓我們有機會先出修補的資安研究員，會在<a href=\"/security/credits/\">安全致謝</a>頁面上被感謝。未跨越安全邊界但被接受的改進，也可能在版本說明中獲得致謝。",
  "Responsible disclosure": "負責任的揭露",
  "Service Park &middot; $2,048": "Service Park &middot; 2,048 USD",
  "So the omakase moved from Ubuntu to Arch, from GNOME to Hyprland, and became <a href=\"/\">Omarchy</a>. Not a layer on top of somebody else&rsquo;s distribution, but the whole meal. Everything Omakub was reaching for, without asking anyone&rsquo;s permission first.": "於是 omakase 從 Ubuntu 搬到 Arch，從 GNOME 搬到 Hyprland，成了<a href=\"/\">Omarchy</a>。不再是疊在別人發行版上的一層，而是整席大餐。Omakub 想夠到的每一樣，這次都不必先問誰准。",
  "Sponsorships": "贊助",
  "Staff": "員工",
  "Steps to reproduce the issue and any proof of concept.": "重現問題的步驟與任何概念驗證。",
  "Thanks to everyone who ran it, contributed to it, and showed off their desktops. Omakub walked so Omarchy could run.": "謝謝跑過它、貢獻過它、曬過桌面的人。Omakub 蹣跚學步，Omarchy 才能奔跑。",
  "The Omacom Foundation employees working full time on Omarchy.": "全職投入 Omarchy 的 Omacom Foundation 員工。",
  "The Perfect Computer may start as omakase, but it&#39;s ultimately yours. Fully and completely. No tollbooths, no gatekeepers, no platforms that can change the terms on you. Just free and open code that you can turn into whatever you desire. The malleable machine of the future is here today and it&#39;s yours to own.": "完美電腦或許始於 omakase，但它終究屬於你。完完全全。沒有收費站，沒有守門人，沒有會片面改規則的平台。只有自由開放的程式碼，任你變成想要的樣子。未來的可塑機器今天就在這裡，屬於你。",
  "The affected component and Omarchy version.": "受影響的元件與 Omarchy 版本。",
  "The age of agents is the most important paradigm shift in computing since the microprocessor, and Omarchy is going to take full advantage. Agents are welcome everywhere. In the code, in the issues, in the pull requests, and in the infrastructure. We&#39;re going to lean all the way in, put the new intelligence to work all over, and together <a href=\"https://wecanfixeverything.com\">We Can Fix Everything</a>!": "代理時代是自微處理器以來運算領域最重要的典範轉移，Omarchy 要吃好吃滿。代理處處受歡迎：程式碼裡、issues 裡、pull request 裡、基礎設施裡。我們要全力押注，讓新的智慧遍地開工，一起<a href=\"https://wecanfixeverything.com\">我們能修好一切</a>！",
  "The entry class. Green foil, gravel flying, and a Quattro heading into the trees. Sixteen bucks gets you on the team.": "入門級別。綠色箔面，碎石飛濺，一台 Quattro 衝進樹林。十六塊錢就能讓你入隊。",
  "The first residents": "第一屆駐站藝術家",
  "The full-time employees of the Omacom Foundation, paid for by <a href=\"/patrons/\">our patrons</a> to make Omarchy better for everyone.": "Omacom Foundation 的全職員工，由<a href=\"/patrons/\">我們的贊助者</a>出資，讓 Omarchy 對所有人更好。",
  "The modern history of computers is barely a lifetime old, but its heritage is rich and deserves our respect. It&#39;s our duty to honor those who forged the path before us. From <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/10307\">shipping basic vi</a> fifty years after Bill Joy wrote the first version to dedicating a <a href=\"https://github.com/dhh/omarchy-giants-theme\">theme to von Neumann</a>. We should be proud of how we got here and make our ancestors smile from retirement or above.": "電腦的現代史不過一輩子長短，但傳承豐厚，值得尊敬。向前人致敬是我們的責任。從 Bill Joy 寫下第一版五十年後<a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/10307\">出貨基礎版 vi</a>，到以<a href=\"https://github.com/dhh/omarchy-giants-theme\">致敬 von Neumann 的佈景主題</a>。我們該為來時路驕傲，讓祖先在退休中或在天上微笑。",
  "The nonprofit funding the development, maintenance, and spread of Omarchy.<br>Interested in becoming a founding or distinguished patron? Write <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>.": "資助 Omarchy 開發、維護與推廣的非營利組織。<br>想成為創始或傑出贊助者？寫信至 <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "The original hacker cred was all about the code. It didn&#39;t care who you were, what your background was, or even if you were legally old enough to operate a <a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2096542976683970838\">three-node elite BBS out of your bedroom</a>. It just cared about the work, the art, the dare. Omarchy is bringing that ethos back, and dropping the Code-of-Conduct struggle sessions and identity-overload nonsense that has plagued open source for far too long. We&#39;re done with all of it. Just be nice and sincere.": "最早的駭客信譽只看程式碼。不看你是誰、什麼背景，甚至不管你年紀夠不夠合法操作<a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2096542976683970838\">臥室裡的三節點菁英 BBS</a>。只看作品、看藝術、看膽識。Omarchy 要帶回這種精神，丟掉困擾開源太久的 Code-of-Conduct 批鬥會和身分超載的胡鬧。那些我們都不要了。友善，真誠，就這樣。",
  "The people and companies funding the development, maintenance, and spread of Omarchy.": "資助 Omarchy 開發、維護與推廣的個人與企業。",
  "The retirement home is staffed": "退休之家有人駐守",
  "The road to Omarchy": "通往 Omarchy 之路",
  "The tiling Wayland compositor that has been at the heart of Omarchy since day one, and one of its three core technologies. The sponsorship lets Vaxry work on it without having to think about commercial development or fundraising - and it freed the existing Hyprperks program to be released for everyone, for free. The deal runs three years, with an option for another two, and starts October 10.": "自第一天起就在 Omarchy 心臟位置的平鋪 Wayland 合成器，也是三大核心技術之一。這筆贊助讓 Vaxry 不必想商業開發或募款，專心做它——連帶讓原本的 Hyprperks 計畫免費開放給所有人。這筆交易為期三年，可再續兩年，自 10 月 10 日起。",
  "The tool that manages the language runtimes and, just as importantly, ships every coding-agent CLI as a lazy-loading stub. A new harness is one command away instead of a packaging project - which is what keeps Omarchy moving at the pace agent tooling actually ships.": "管理語言執行環境的工具，更重要的是，它把每個 coding-agent CLI 都做成延遲載入樁。新的代理框架一道指令就到，不必搞打包工程——這正是 Omarchy 跟上代理工具出貨速度的原因。",
  "There are amazing nerds everywhere. Cracked teenagers. Wise neckbeards. Obsessive people with jagged opinions and incredible talent. But we&#39;re spread across a thousand little fiefdoms, accomplishing a fraction of what we could together. Omarchy is a rallying cry to unite that talent behind a common goal: Make Linux win the desktop, as the prophecy foretold.": "厲害的 nerd 到處都是。天才少年。睿智的老鬍子。偏執、難搞但才華橫溢的人。但我們散落在上千個小諸侯國，各自只發揮了合力的一小部分。Omarchy 是集結號，把這些才華團結到共同目標下：讓 Linux 贏得桌面，如預言所言。",
  "There&#39;s no paper cut too small, no incompatibility too difficult, and no partnership that&#39;s out of reach. Omarchy&#39;s mission is nothing less than <em>The Perfect Computer</em>. That means <a href=\"https://x.com/mitchellh/status/2074225453217505494\">the pursuit of excellence without justification</a>. Everything should be faster, better, prettier. We can do all of it, at the same time, and be done before ASI.": "沒有小到不值得修的小毛病，沒有難到修不好的不相容，沒有攀不上的合作。Omarchy 的使命只有一個：<em>完美電腦</em>。也就是<a href=\"https://x.com/mitchellh/status/2074225453217505494\">不為自己辯解的卓越追求</a>。一切都要更快、更好、更美。我們能同時做到全部，在 ASI 到來前完工。",
  "There's only so much you can do with GNOME, but I did what I could.": "GNOME 能做的就這麼多，但我已盡力。",
  "They found it, told us privately, and waited for the patch": "他們發現了它，私下告訴我們，並等待修補程式",
  "Three of the themes that ship with Omarchy are his - <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Lumon, Miasma, and Retro 82</a> - and another ten sit on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a>, from Batman to City-783 to Sakura Mochi. He works in whole palettes rather than one-off colour schemes, which is why his themes hold together across the terminal, Neovim, btop, and the shell instead of just looking good in a screenshot.": "隨 Omarchy 出貨的三套佈景主題出自他手——<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Lumon、Miasma 與 Retro 82</a>——另有十套在<a href=\"/themes/\">附錄頁面</a>上，從 Batman、City-783 到 Sakura Mochi。他以整套色盤創作，而非一次性配色，因此他的佈景主題在終端機、Neovim、btop 與 shell 中都協調一致，而不只在截圖裡好看。",
  "Trademark": "商標",
  "Violet foil under the floodlights of the service park, where the car gets rebuilt between stages. Two thousand dollars keeps a lot of open-source developers in the race.": "維修區燈光下的紫色箔面，賽車在站與站之間於此重建。兩千美元讓許多開源開發者留在賽道上。",
  "We consider a bug a security vulnerability when it can be exploited to cross a meaningful security boundary: an untrusted or lower-privileged party gains access, permissions, or control they didn&rsquo;t already have.": "當 bug 可被利用來跨越有意義的安全邊界——不受信任或低權限的一方取得了原本沒有的存取、權限或控制——我們就視為安全漏洞。",
  "We&#39;re serious people, doing serious work, but if we can&#39;t laugh at ourselves and the delusional mission, it gets stuffy and stale real quick. We need fun, we need whimsy, we need cool for its own sake. The computer needs easter eggs, it needs silly games, it needs <a href=\"https://radio.omarchy.org\">funny pun songs</a>. Serious people have serious fun.": "我們是認真做事的認真人，但要是連自己和這個妄想級使命都不能笑一笑，氣氛很快就又悶又僵。我們需要樂趣，需要奇想，需要為酷而酷。電腦需要彩蛋，需要蠢遊戲，需要<a href=\"https://radio.omarchy.org\">諧音哏歌曲</a>。認真的人，認真玩。",
  "We&rsquo;ll review your report and keep you informed as we&rsquo;re able while we work toward a resolution.": "我們會審查你的回報，並在處理過程中盡可能讓你知道進度。",
  "What is a vulnerability?": "什麼是漏洞？",
  "What it comes with": "內含什麼",
  "What to include": "應包含什麼",
  "Wordmark": "字標",
  "Write <a href=\"mailto:foundation@omarchy.org\">foundation@omarchy.org</a> for partnerships.": "合作洽詢請寫信至 <a href=\"mailto:foundation@omarchy.org\">foundation@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "You don't need a new computer to try Omarchy. Give the one you already have a second life.": "試用 Omarchy 不需要新電腦。讓你手邊這台重獲新生吧。",
  "Your preferred contact details for follow-up.": "你偏好的後續聯絡方式。",
  "outfoxxed created <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a>, the toolkit behind Omarchy Shell. He makes the desktop faster, more reliable, and easier for people and agents to extend through plugins. He also serves on <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a>.": "outfoxxed 打造了<a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a>——Omarchy Shell 背後的工具包。他讓桌面更快、更可靠，也讓人們與代理更容易透過外掛擴展它。他同時擔任<a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a> 成員。"
}
